  "feature": "Deck analysis \u2014 the findings and their receipt (PR 4c)",
  "note": "\"What is in this deck\": five findings, the receipt modal behind each one that has cards, the card modal stacked on it, and the provenance panel. Same preconditions as `deck-verdict.json`, and read that file's note first: the server needs ANALYSIS_TAB_ENABLED=true, every row reaches the tab by a PRESS, and every deck id must belong to the signed-in account.\n\nTWO DECKS. FINDINGS_DECK is `d0000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000cafe` on `local-dev`, which holds game changers and tutors and draws the card-list receipt. COMBO_DECK is `d0000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000c0b0`, built for this sheet on 2026-09-22 because no deck the e2e account owned assembled a combo, so the combo body had no cell: Kess, Dissident Mage leading Mirror of Fate and Thassa's Oracle, Spellbook variant `1164-1295`. It is trivial to rebuild: the deck needs its commander and those two `deck_cards` rows, nothing more.\n\nTHE STACKED ROW is the one that matters at 390. Since stacked sheets R1 the card REPLACES the receipt on the phone, drawn at its unstacked size with `← {sheet}` in the ✕'s slot; `stacked-sheets.json` photographs every such pair.\n\nNO `shares` BLOCK: the findings and the receipt are mounted by `analysis-panel.tsx` alone.",
